# System Architecture — polyglot-chat-architecture

## Overview

A polyglot real-time chat system split across two backend services and one frontend.
**The goal is to show Go skills** — Go owns auth, channels, and WebSocket broadcast.
Node.js owns only what it does uniquely well: DM Socket.IO and media upload.

---

## Service Map

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  React + Vite  (port 5173)                                       │
│                                                                  │
│  axios ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│    └─→ Go service :8080  (auth + channels REST)              │   │
│                                                              │   │
│  Socket.IO client ───────────────────────────────────────┐  │   │
│    └─→ Node.js :5000  (DM real-time)                     │  │   │
│                                                          │  │   │
│  raw WebSocket ───────────────────────────────────────┐  │  │   │
│    └─→ Go service :8080  ws://...  (channel real-time)│  │  │   │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──┴──┴───┘
                            │                │            │
          ┌─────────────────┘                │            │
          ▼                                  ▼            ▼
┌─────────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Go service :8080   │         │  Node.js chat-service :5000        │
│                     │         │                                    │
│  /auth/register     │         │  Socket: login_me                  │
│  /auth/login        │         │  Socket: send_message              │
│  /auth/me           │         │  Socket: send_media                │
│                     │  Redis  │  REST:   /conversation/*           │
│  /channels          │◄───────►│                                    │
│  /channels/:id/join │ Pub/Sub │  Subscribes to channel:* topics    │
│  /channels/:id/msg  │         │  ← fans out to Socket.IO rooms     │
│                     │         │                                    │
│  ws://.../channels  │         │  Verifies JWT (shared secret)      │
│  goroutine/channel  │         │                                    │
│  Redis Pub/Sub pub  │         └────────────────────┬───────────────┘
│                     │                              │
│  Issues JWT ────────┼── JWT_SECRET (shared env) ───┘
└──────┬──────────────┘
       │               
       ▼               
┌─────────────┐    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│  PostgreSQL │    │  MongoDB                             │
│  (Go owns)  │    │  (Node.js owns)                      │
│  users      │    │  conversations  (DMs)                │
│  channels   │    │  ← Node reads user _id from JWT      │
│  channel_   │    │    never queries Postgres directly   │
│  members    │    └──────────────────────────────────────┘
│  channel_   │
│  messages   │    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
└─────────────┘    │  Redis                               │
                   │  online:<userId>       (presence)    │
                   │  channel:<channelId>   (Pub/Sub)     │
                   │  ch_members:<chId>     (set)         │
                   └──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Service Responsibilities

### Go service (`go-service/`)

| Area | What |
|------|------|
| **Auth** | `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, `GET /auth/me` |
| **JWT** | Issues tokens signed with `JWT_SECRET`. Validates its own tokens. |
| **Channels REST** | Create channel, join by invite link, list messages |
| **Channels WS** | `ws://:8080/ws/channels/:id` — goroutine per channel hub |
| **Broadcast** | Goroutine hub per channel + Redis Pub/Sub for future horizontal scale |
| **DB** | PostgreSQL via `pgx` |

> **One binary, two internal packages**: `internal/auth` and `internal/channels`.
> Split into two binaries only if they need independent scaling.

---

### Node.js service (`backend/`)

| Area | What |
|------|------|
| **DM messaging** | Socket.IO `send_message`, `send_media` |
| **Presence** | `login_me` → Redis, `disconnect` → Redis cleanup |
| **Channel relay** | Subscribes to Redis `channel:*` Pub/Sub → fans out via Socket.IO |
| **Media upload** | `POST /conversation/media` via Multer |
| **History** | `POST /conversation/from-to` |
| **JWT validation** | Verifies tokens issued by Go (same `JWT_SECRET`) |
| **DB** | MongoDB via Mongoose |

> Node.js does **not** create users or channels. It trusts the JWT for identity.

---

## Database Design

### PostgreSQL (Go service)

```sql
-- users
id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
name        TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL
password    TEXT NOT NULL          -- bcrypt hash
created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()

-- channels
id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
name        TEXT NOT NULL
type        TEXT NOT NULL          -- 'open' | 'private'
invite_code TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL   -- random slug, shareable link
owner_id    UUID REFERENCES users(id)
created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()

-- channel_members
channel_id  UUID REFERENCES channels(id)
user_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id)
joined_at   TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
PRIMARY KEY (channel_id, user_id)

-- channel_messages
id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
channel_id  UUID REFERENCES channels(id)
user_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id)
body        TEXT
media_url   TEXT
created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
```

### MongoDB (Node.js)

```
conversations  { from, to, body, media_url, createdAt, updatedAt }
```

> Users are identified by their UUID from the JWT — Node never stores or queries users.

---

## JWT Design

```json
{
  "id":   "<postgres uuid>",
  "name": "rakesh",
  "iat":  1710000000,
  "exp":  1710604800
}
```

- Both services share `JWT_SECRET` via environment variable.
- Go issues the token. Node verifies it with the same secret.
- Go WebSocket upgrade also validates the token from the `Authorization` header (or query param `?token=...` for WS handshake).

---

## Channel WebSocket Flow

```
Client                       Go (channel hub)              Redis
  │                               │                          │
  ├── WS connect /ws/channels/:id │                          │
  │   Authorization: Bearer <jwt> │                          │
  │                               │ validate JWT             │
  │                               │ register conn in hub     │
  │                               │                          │
  ├── {"type":"message","body":"hi"}                         │
  │                               │ save to PostgreSQL       │
  │                               │ PUBLISH channel:<id> ───►│
  │                               │                          │
  │◄── {"type":"message",...} ────┤◄─── (go hub broadcast)  │
  │                               │                          │
  │         (Node subscriber)     │         Redis            │
  │◄── Socket.IO "channel_msg" ───│◄─── SUBSCRIBE channel:* ─┤
```

---

## Invite Link Flow (Private Channels)

```
Creator               Go service             Joiner
  │                       │                    │
  ├─ POST /channels ──────►│                    │
  │   { name, type }       │ generate uuid +    │
  │◄── { invite_code } ────┤ random invite_code │
  │                        │ save to Postgres   │
  │                        │                    │
  │  shares link: /join?code=<invite_code>      │
  │                        │◄───────────────────┤
  │                        │ POST /channels/join │
  │                        │ { invite_code }     │
  │                        │ insert channel_member
  │                        │────────────────────►│
  │                        │◄─{ channel_id, ... }│
```

